# Build artifacts
.pio/
.pioenvs/
.piolibdeps/
build/

# IDE files
.vscode/.browse.c_cpp.db*
.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/ipch
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Compiled files
*.o
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex
*.uf2
*.map

# Device backups — a .bkp is a full LittleFS dump and carries /config/system.bin
# (Wi-Fi/MQTT/API secrets + password hashes). Never commit one. Finding C-1
# (2026-08-16): a device.bkp was once committed; history has since been purged
# with git filter-repo and the exposed credentials rotated. The rule stays.
*.bkp

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Generated assets
WebUI_GZ.h
src/WebUI_GZ.h

# Generated docs
docs/MANUAL.html
docs/MANUAL.pdf
docs/MANUAL_with_images.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Test server certs (self-signed)
tools/test-server/certs/

# Test reports and logs (generated at runtime)
docs/test_reports/

# Screenshots (generated)
docs/screenshots_v2/
docs/screenshots_v4/

# Device runtime data (generated on-device)
data/history/
data/config/
# data/web holds the output of a per-env page diet (custom_fs_pages, see
# tools/build_webui_gz.py). Nothing in it is tracked, and from 2026-08-17
# nothing in it ships: a shipping image carries every page in flash, so these
# are build artifacts of the instrumented env alone — written by the build that
# asks for them, uploaded to the bench unit by hand.
#
# They were tracked for one release, while the release image depended on them.
# That is also the release where no zip actually carried them and /license
# shipped broken, which is the argument for not letting a user's image depend
# on a file that has to be deployed separately.
data/web/
# Contents, not the directory — git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a negation inside one never matches.
data/themes/*
# ...except the curated collection itself, which is authored source (built by
# tools/gen_theme_collection.py, contrast-audited) and is what docs/MANUAL.md
# links to. Only themes the device writes at runtime stay out.
!data/themes/*.thm
data/calib.csv
data/system.blog
data/system.old.blog
data/*.blog

# Claude Code (local state may contain machine paths; the shared project
# settings file stays tracked)
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json

# Changelogs (auto-generated or versioned)
CHANGELOG_*.md

# Promotion (local only, not for the repo)
docs/promotion/

# Nothing under release/ is history — it is all output. The zips are the
# GitHub release assets, and the simut_{tft,alpha,pio} trees are the staging
# dirs those zips are built from: tools/build_release*.sh does `rm -rf` and
# rsyncs them from source on every run, and nothing outside those scripts
# reads them. Versioning them cost 26 MB and a second copy of every document
# to keep in sync — a docs fix had to be applied twice or wait for the next
# release. Untracked 2026-08-21; git history keeps the old copies, and the
# build scripts still write here exactly as before.
release/

# local bench scratch
scratchpad/

# libFuzzer local findings (tools/run_fuzz.sh)
crash-*
leak-*
slow-unit-*
oom-*

# Bench-generated artifacts (telemetry bench + browser campaign tools)
tools/telemetry_bench/certs/
tools/telemetry_bench/results/
tools/shots/
